<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01439#audience_id> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme is designed for a broad, general internet audience familiar with internet humor, visual puns, and common idioms. It relies on cultural knowledge of the idiom 'get the goat' and the ability to appreciate absurd wordplay and visual juxtaposition, which are common elements in meme culture. There are no specific demographic, cultural, or community markers that target a narrow group; the humor is accessible to anyone who understands the basic English idiom and can interpret the visual pun. The meme is lighthearted and non-toxic, making it suitable for a wide range of users without requiring specific background knowledge beyond general internet literacy."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#perimeterFraming> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Indicates text surrounding visual content as a frame or border in memes"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#DimensionsAlignment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relationships where dimensions mutually reinforce and amplify each other's meaning in memes"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#metaphoricallyMapsTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Indicates metaphorical or analogical mapping between dimension instances"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#User> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#DramaticIrony> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "One dimension revealing information another dimension does not provide in memes, e.g. text revealing information visuals don't show"@en .
_:na36c737a1ca84d419f612ab2c9f0cbd9b22 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#Semi-transparentOverlay> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Text that blends with underlying visual content through transparency in memes"@en .
