<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01439#overallintent_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "meme-id: im_long_and_strong; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image depicts two goats on a rocky terrain, with one goat mounted on the other. The text overlay reads 'im long and strong and down to get the goat hump on.' This meme uses a visual pun, juxtaposing the literal physical act of mating goats with the idiomatic phrase 'get the goat,' which means to annoy or irritate someone. The humor is derived from the double meaning and the absurdity of the situation. There is no toxicity present in this meme. The intent is purely comedic and relies on wordplay and visual juxtaposition, not on targeting any specific group or promoting harmful content. The meme is a harmless, lighthearted joke that plays on the literal interpretation of a common idiom."@en .
