<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#DirectSuperimposition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Text or elements directly overlaid on top of other content in memes"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TemplateStructure> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Underlying structural patterns and organizational frameworks of memes"@en .
_:na36c737a1ca84d419f612ab2c9f0cbd9b32 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TextualMaterial> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01439#goat_mating_behavior> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The visual of one goat mounted on another is a literal depiction of mating behavior. The humor of the meme relies on the juxtaposition of this biological act with the idiom 'get the goat,' which is unrelated to animals. Understanding the biological context of goat mating is necessary to appreciate the visual pun."@en .
